id: pm-unit-exact-conversion
title: Convert admitted exact quantities without intermediate overflow
description: "Issue #6: identity conversion must normalize directly, and compatible-unit scaling must reduce the factor ratio before multiplying. Reject only oversized exact final results; cover both component boundaries and public SDK read paths."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-unit#6"
created_at: "2026-11-06T17:49:46.669Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T17:54:14.226Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-sol
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T17:50:14.937Z",codex-sol,"Confirmed main 0578835 still fails: built public convert returns limit_exceeded for 80-digit GB and h identity conversions; m identity succeeds. Source applies checked source-to-base multiplication before destination division. Plan: normalize identity directly, reduce source/destination factor ratio before one multiplication, and verify both component boundaries with an independent oracle plus real SDK non-git tracker reads."
  "2026-11-06T17:51:09.554Z",codex-sol,"Failing-test proof before the fix: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/conversion-boundary.test.ts failed all three tests (identity property, compatible-unit oracle property, real SDK conversion/self-comparison). Implemented direct rational normalization for identity and one multiplication by the pre-reduced scale ratio; no precision threshold changed."
  "2026-11-06T17:54:14.224Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: node test/revert.acceptance.ts --conversion-only reports EXPECTED FAIL independently for boundary identity, boundary compatible and boundary SDK when only convert is replaced with main behavior in disposable copies. Targeted tests pass 3/3 with 6518 fitting and 2762 oversized distinct-unit oracle cases; npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run duplication and npm run docstring pass. Real non-git SDK coverage additionally exercises cross-unit comparison, persisted subtraction and uncertainty conversion. Full npm and Bun release gates and queued bot review remain required before handoff."
